  :how "Two mechanical passes over negative_controls.sh, no full 5-10 min run needed. (1) PLANT-LANDED: for every plant step (sed/edn/python mutation), execute the mutation alone into a temp copy and diff against its source; require a non-empty diff AND, for key-addressed plants (assoc-in [:rows N ...], maps keyed by :name/:id), require the addressed key to exist (parse the EDN, check (get-in d path) or the predicate match count >= 1). Flag any sed whose pattern count in the source file is 0 -- that is 13o/14j caught at audit time, not publish time. (2) VACUITY PROBE: for every negative control, run its checker on the UNPLANTED source and evaluate the control's own assertion grep against that output; if the assertion already holds on the good artifact, the control cannot distinguish planted from unplanted and controls nothing (catches the 14l mode and the generic-grep mode of 6b/6a/8o). (3) DEAD-ASSERTION scan: flag any test of the form [ \"$(cmd)\" = \"$(same cmd)\" ] and any pin grep whose pattern is a literal that also occurs in the checker's boilerplate/usage text."
